.TH XD\-EFFECTS 1 2026-10-26 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-effects \- Desktop Effects
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-effects
.OP \-\-effect id
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xd\-effects
is the Desktop Effects applet (Control Panel > Appearance and Themes):
the compositor's animated effects for windows and the desktop, laid out as
CompizConfig Settings Manager was.
.TP
.B Side bar
A Filter box, which finds effects by their name, description or options
(Enter opens the only one found); the categories (All, Effects, Window
Management, Desktop, Accessibility, Utility); Preferences; and Close.
.TP
.B Effects
Every effect under its category, with its icon, its name and a check box
that turns it on or off at once.
Clicking an effect opens its page.
.TP
.B An effect's page
Its description, Use this effect, and its options (on tabs when it has
many), each with a button that puts it back to its default; Back (or Esc)
returns to the effects.
Key and mouse button bindings are set by pressing them; screen edges and
corners by choosing them.
.TP
.B Preferences
Whether to warn when an effect turned on, or a binding chosen, uses the
same key, mouse button or screen edge as another effect that is on; and
Reset All, which turns every effect off and sets their options back to
their defaults.
.PP
Every effect is off at first.
Changes are saved as they are made, in
.BR ~/.config/xeondesktop/effects.ini ,
which
.BR xd\-compositor (1)
watches and applies at once.
.PP
Effects drawn with OpenGL (Wobbly Windows) need
.BR xd\-compositor\-fx (1)
drawing with OpenGL ES; under the plain compositor, in software rendering
or a virtual machine they are greyed out with the reason, which the
compositor gives in
.BR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/xeondesktop/effects\-$WAYLAND_DISPLAY.ini .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-effect " id"
Open that effect's page; the ids are effects.ini's group names, such as
.BR WobblyWindows .
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/xeondesktop/effects.ini
One group per effect:
.B Enabled=
and the options that differ from their defaults; keys this version does
not know are kept.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xd\-compositor (1),
.BR xd\-compositor\-fx (1),
.BR xd\-control (1),
.BR xd\-desk (1)
